This script acts as a stealthy surveillance tool designed to capture and exfiltrate a screenshot from a compromised computer. It first generates a unique filename using the computer's name, a random number, and a timestamp to avoid overwriting files. Using built-in .NET libraries, it takes a screenshot of the entire virtual screen and stores the image directly in memory instead of saving it to the disk, which helps avoid detection. The image is then converted into a base64 text string so it can be easily embedded and sent over the internet. Finally, the script silently transmits this encoded image data, along with its details, to a remote command-and-control (C2) server via a standard HTTP POST request, allowing an attacker to remotely monitor the user's activity.